  finding bars/badges/clocks by colour search, which the model now does as native classes.
  Keep while the onnx path is still selectable; retire with it.

The hybrid worth building either way: the model gives a bar's BOUNDING BOX, not its fill %.
Best architecture is model-localizes -> existing pixel logic reads the fill inside. That
deletes every hardcoded tower coordinate, which is what caused all three EMPTY_BGR bugs
this session.

